# For working on Firetower from a checkout. Copy to .env and fill in what you
# need — every value here has a working default, which is the difference
# between this file and deploy/.env.example, where three of them have none.
#
# Running Firetower rather than building it uses that other one. See the README.
#
# Firetower reads ./.env, then ~/.firetower/.env.
#
# Nothing here is a credential. Those go in the secret store, encrypted — so if
# you ever find yourself putting one here, something has gone wrong.

# Authorizing GitHub is no longer configured here — the interface asks for a
# client id in the setup wizard, and again on the connect-a-repository screen,
# and keeps it in the database.

# The control plane's database. `just dev` starts one from compose.yaml;
# this is where to point it somewhere else.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://firetower:firetower@localhost:5433/firetower

# What compose creates the database with.
# POSTGRES_USER=firetower
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=firetower
# POSTGRES_DB=firetower
# POSTGRES_PORT=5433

# The key every stored credential is encrypted with, base64, 32 bytes.
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# That is the whole of it — 44 characters ending in `=`. Anything else is
# refused at start-up rather than used, because a key that is not a key would
# seal every credential under junk.
#
# Set this and nothing is written to disk — which is what a container or a
# server wants. Leave it unset and Firetower keeps one at ~/.firetower/root.key,
# mode 0600, created on first run. Either way it lives outside the database, so
# a database backup on its own opens nothing.
#
# Losing it means adding every credential again. Back it up separately.
# FIRETOWER_ROOT_KEY=

# Who to create as the administrator on a database with no users. Both
# optional: with neither, one is made and its password printed once at start-up.
# ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
# ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD=

# Where Firetower keeps its state. Defaults to ~/.firetower
# FIRETOWER_HOME=

# The port the control plane listens on. Defaults to 4400
# FIRETOWER_PORT=
